GOAL: Fix a bug in /luxon/src/impl/util.js in the function `objToLocalTS` (around line 155) so that `DateTime#plus` works across the year-100 barrier when the addition passes through February. The expected behaviour is that adding days to a date in year 99 produces the correct proleptic-Gregorian result in year 100 (year 100 is NOT a leap year, while year 2000 IS).

CURRENT CODE:

    // covert a calendar object to a local timestamp (epoch, but with the offset baked in)
    export function objToLocalTS(obj) {
      let d = Date.UTC(
        obj.year,
        obj.month - 1,
        obj.day,
        obj.hour,
        obj.minute,
        obj.second,
        obj.millisecond
      );

      // for legacy reasons, years between 0 and 99 are interpreted as 19XX; revert that
      if (obj.year < 100 && obj.year >= 0) {
        d = new Date(d);
        d.setUTCFullYear(d.getUTCFullYear() - 1900);
      }
      return +d;
    }

WHY IT IS WRONG: `Date.UTC(99, 11, 92)` is computed as 1999-12-92, i.e. it rolls over using year 2000 (a leap year) giving 2000-03-01. Subtracting 1900 from the resulting year then yields 0100-03-01. But the correct answer for "0099-12-31 plus 61 days" is 0100-03-02, because year 100 is not a leap year (February 100 has 28 days, whereas February 2000 has 29). The day/month rollover must be recomputed with the real target year.

REQUIRED FIX (minimal; change only this function):

    // covert a calendar object to a local timestamp (epoch, but with the offset baked in)
    export function objToLocalTS(obj) {
      let d = Date.UTC(
        obj.year,
        obj.month - 1,
        obj.day,
        obj.hour,
        obj.minute,
        obj.second,
        obj.millisecond
      );

      // for legacy reasons, years between 0 and 99 are interpreted as 19XX; revert that
      if (obj.year < 100 && obj.year >= 0) {
        d = new Date(d);
        // set the month and day again, this is necessary because year 2000 is a leap year, but year 100 is not
        // so if obj.year is in 99, but obj.day makes it roll over into year 100,
        // the calculations done by Date.UTC are using year 2000 - which is leap, and year 100 is not
        d.setUTCFullYear(obj.year, obj.month - 1, obj.day);
      }
      return +d;
    }

Do not change anything else in /luxon/src/impl/util.js or any other source file.

