GOAL: Fix a bug in the `isInDST` getter in /luxon/src/datetime.js (around line 1164) so that DateTimes inside a DST period are correctly reported as being in DST, including the special case of the 1974 year-round DST in the USA (which ran from January 6, 1974 to October 27, 1974).

CURRENT CODE:

    /**
     * Get whether the DateTime is in a DST.
     * @type {boolean}
     */
    get isInDST() {
      if (this.isOffsetFixed) {
        return false;
      } else {
        return (
          this.offset > this.set({ month: 1 }).offset || this.offset > this.set({ month: 5 }).offset
        );
      }
    }

WHY IT IS WRONG: `this.set({ month: 1 })` keeps the current day-of-month, so for a DateTime that is already in January it returns the same instant and the comparison is degenerate. Example: `DateTime.fromISO("1974-02-15", { zone: "America/New_York" })` is in DST (offset -240) but `set({month: 1})` gives 1974-02-15 itself (offset -240) and `set({month: 5})` gives 1974-06-15 (offset -240), so `isInDST` wrongly returns false. Comparing against January 1st of the same year fixes this, because Jan 1 1974 is standard time (offset -300).

REQUIRED FIX (minimal; change only the `isInDST` getter, keep the doc comment):

    get isInDST() {
      if (this.isOffsetFixed) {
        return false;
      } else {
        return (
          this.offset > this.set({ month: 1, day: 1 }).offset ||
          this.offset > this.set({ month: 5 }).offset
        );
      }
    }

